# Holdout Cases
This directory will contain the 30 **frozen** holdout cases for AOA-Bench.

---

## 📌 Purpose
Holdout cases are used to:
1. Evaluate AOA’s performance **after tuning** on the development set.
2. Ensure the model generalizes to unseen cases.
3. Serve as the **final gate** before release.

---

## ⚠️ Rules
1. **No Modifications**: Holdout cases **must not** be modified after freezing.
2. **No Tuning**: AOA’s semantic components **must not** be tuned using holdout cases.
3. **Freeze Before Tuning**: Holdout cases must be frozen **before** any semantic tuning begins.

---

## 📁 Structure
Organize cases into subdirectories by category (same as `dev/`):

```
benchmark/holdout/
├── arithmetic/
│   ├── case-001.json
│   ├── case-002.json
│   └── ...
├── facts/
│   ├── case-001.json
│   └── ...
├── citations/
│   ├── case-001.json
│   └── ...
├── contradictions/
│   ├── case-001.json
│   └── ...
├── judgment/
│   ├── case-001.json
│   └── ...
└── clean/
    ├── case-001.json
    └── ...
```

---

## 📝 Case Naming Convention
- Use the format: `case-[ID].json` (e.g., `case-001.json`).
- Assign IDs sequentially (e.g., `AOA-HOLD-001`, `AOA-HOLD-002`).

---

## 🚀 Next Steps
1. Populate this directory with 30 holdout cases.
2. Freeze the cases by setting `"holdout_frozen": true` in `benchmark/manifest.json`.
3. Run AOA on the holdout set to evaluate performance.

---

## 📊 Gates
AOA v0.1 **cannot** be released until all of the following gates pass on the holdout set:

- [ ] **Material-Defect Recall**: ≥75%
- [ ] **High-Severity Finding Precision**: ≥85%
- [ ] **Deterministic Arithmetic Correctness**: 100%
- [ ] **Supported Findings with Evidence**: 100%
- [ ] **Judgment-Dependent Routing**: 100%

